[0.071, "o", "\u001b[?2026h\u001b[3;1H\u001b[K\u001b[Cbudget and interests—art, history, food, classical music, nightlife, or        \u001b[4;2Hsomething else?    \r\n\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[48;2;33;59;73m                                                                                \u001b[49m\u001b[7;1H\u001b[K\u001b[48;2;33;59;73m \u001b[38;2;222;224;225mTell me a historical fact about Vienna that few people know.\u001b[39m                   \u001b[8;1H                                                                                \u001b[49m\u001b[9;1H\u001b[K\r\n\u001b[K\u001b[CVienna once had a wall made partly from\u001b[Ccaptured Ottoman gravestones. After    \u001b[11;1H\u001b[K\u001b[Cthe failed Ottoman siege of 1529, some tombstones were reportedly reused to    \u001b[12;1H\u001b[K\u001b[Cstrengthen city defenses—an eerie example of the city recycling the physical   \u001b[13;2Htraces of its enemies.                 \u001b[1;44H\u001b[?2026l"]
